{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790362077,"nonce":"ZezJRwthI6uTTxQbueMx2EPe/2s=","title":"ZynML async composition tests only compile with a feature that is off by default","message":"Most async composition tests in crates/zynml are gated on zynml's own `krio-async-backend` feature, which is off by default, so a default `cargo test -p zynml` and CI never build or run them, although the runtime always lowers async through krio. Ungate them (or gate on what actually selects the path) so the async, effect and fiber composition tests run on every CI lane.","files":null}]}